id=dirtysepbypass
name=DirtySepolicy Bypass
version=v5.0.1
versionCode=50001
author=SHuiTU68
description=Kernel-side hiding (no Zygisk). A kprobe LKM hides Magisk/LSPosed/KernelSU/APatch SELinux contexts and fakes selinuxfs access answers for ordinary apps; mount-table hiding is opt-in. The module loads after boot (service stage) with a panic guard, so a failure cannot keep the device from booting. Requires arm64 and a 6.6 GKI kernel that allows kretprobes and unsigned modules.
updateJson=
